// A blast at the end of a flooded trough throws the water up and away: the pool is backed by its bed, so
// it heaves up out of the trough in a plume of spray that rains back down. No water is lost (a cell or two
// drains into the granite bed the charge cracked under it).
map
################################
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#..............................#
#.@............................#
#####......................#####
#####wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww#####
#####wwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww#####
################################
end
expect 1 count:Water == 44
explode 5 4 2 0.25               // in the water at the trough's left end
expect 6 is:4,2,Water == 0       // blown out of the near end
expect 6 is:12,2,Water == 0      // the surface heaved right along the trough
expect 6 debris:Water > 30       // most of the pool is in the air
expect 6 count:Water < 14
expect 120 debris:Water == 0     // and it has all come down again
expect 240 count:Water > 43
